   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\"><div><br><br>On May 13, 2011, at 5:54 AM, Mohamed ElSoda &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">elsoda....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br></div><div></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\">Dear Karl,</span></div>\n\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\">I am using r/qtl to make a map for Brassica F7 RIL population. It is recognized as F2 &quot;I think that should be ok?&quot;.</span></div>\n\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN:0cm 0cm 10pt\"></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\"><div>I think no; you want to use convert2riself() to convert to cross type &quot;riself&quot;. This will also drop het genotypes.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\"><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\">I used this script</span></div>\n\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\">\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\">Map &lt;- read.cross(&quot;csv&quot;, &quot;M:/R-qtl&quot;, &quot;Map.csv&quot;, na.strings=&quot;na&quot;,genotypes=c(&quot;a&quot;,&quot;h&quot;,&quot;b&quot;),alleles=c(&quot;a&quot;,&quot;b&quot;), estimate.map=FALSE),   </span><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\">but I got this </span></div>\n</span><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\">warnning message </span></div>\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\"><font color=\"#cc0000\">In summary.cross(cross) : <br>\n    Some chromosomes &gt; 1000 cM in length; there may be a problem with the genetic map. <br>    (Perhaps it is in basepairs?) <br></font></span></div>\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN:0cm 0cm 10pt\"> I tried your reply to a previouse question by using <span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\"><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\">(estimate.map, replace.map), but it didn&#39;t help. </span></span></div>\n\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\"><span style=\"FONT-SIZE:10pt;LINE-HEIGHT:115%;FONT-FAMILY:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,&#39;serif&#39;\">Any advice?</span></span></div>\n\n\n</div></blockquote><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\"><div>In what way did it not work?  An error message?  </div><div><br></div><div>It may be that there are problem markers that are leading to big gaps in the map and need to be removed.</div><div><br></div><div>karl</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "IlFXJczQcp4J",
   "from": "Mohamed ElSoda",
   "author": "8a4064f0ec469c07",
   "date": "2012-03-04T21:07:35Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Rqtl-disc] Mapping in R/qtl",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Dear Karl, </div><div> </div><div>I am trying to get a heatmap using LOD scores. </div><div>I am using these scripts </div><div> </div><div><font size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\">\nx &lt;- read.csv(&quot;bath&quot;)</span></code></p><font size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\">row.names(x)\n&lt;- x$Name</span></code></p><font size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\">\nx&lt;- x[,4:20]<span>  </span></span></code></p><font size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\">x</span></code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\">_matrix &lt;- data.matrix(x</span><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\">)</span></p>\n<font size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\">x_matrix &lt;- t(x)</span></p><font size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\n\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\">heatmap(as.matrix(</span><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\">x</span></code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\">_matrix,nrow(</span><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\">x</span></code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\">_matrix),ncol(</span><code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\">x</span></code><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;font-size:10pt\">_matrix)),Colv=NA)</span></p>\n<font size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\n\n</font></div><div>1-How can I set colours based on LOD scores (-6 to -4 = green), (-4 to -2 blue), (-2 to 2 = white), (2 to 4 = yellow), (4 to 6 = red)?</div><div>2- How to put a bar with colour scale?</div><div> </div><div>\nThanks in advance,</div><div> </div><div>Mohamed</div><div> </div>\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "LDti2EIUshMJ",
   "from": "Karl Broman",
   "author": "96353e7106735838",
   "date": "2012-03-04T21:52:31Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Rqtl-disc] Mapping in R/qtl",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Your question isn&#39;t related to R/qtl, but I&#39;ll attempt to answer it anyway.<p>I&#39;ve never used the function heatmap(), but I expect it&#39;s similar to image(), for which you&#39;d specify colors with the argument &#39;col&#39; and intervals with &#39;breaks&#39;, like the following:<p>  x &lt;- matrix(runif(100, -6, 6), ncol=10)<br>  colorpal &lt;- c(&quot;green&quot;,&quot;blue&quot;,&quot;white&quot;,&quot;yellow&quot;,&quot;red&quot;)<br>  brks &lt;- c(-6, -4, -2, 2, 4, 6)<br>  image(x, col=colorpal, breaks=brks)<p>To get a color scale, I&#39;ve generally used layout() to create two side-by-sdie<p>  layout(cbind(1,2), width=c(6,1))<p>  colorpal &lt;- c(&quot;green&quot;,&quot;blue&quot;,&quot;white&quot;,&quot;yellow&quot;,&quot;red&quot;)<br>  brks &lt;- c(-6, -4, -2, 2, 4, 6)<br>  image(x, col=colorpal, breaks=brks)<p>  v &lt;- seq(-6, 6, length=251)<br>  image(1, v, matrix(v, nrow=1), col=colorpal, breaks=brks, ylab=&quot;&quot;, xaxt=&quot;n&quot;, xlab=&quot;&quot;)<br> <br>karl<p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<p><p><p><p><p><p><p>On Mar 4, 2012, at 3:07 PM, Mohamed ElSoda wrote:</p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<p><p><p><p><p><p><p><p>&gt; Dear Karl,<br>&gt;  <br>&gt; I am trying to get a heatmap using LOD scores.<br>&gt; I am using these scripts<br>&gt;  <br>&gt; x &lt;- read.csv(&quot;bath&quot;)<br>&gt; <br>&gt; row.names(x) &lt;- x$Name<br>&gt; <br>&gt; x&lt;- x[,4:20] <br>&gt; <br>&gt; x_matrix &lt;- data.matrix(x)<br>&gt; <br>&gt; x_matrix &lt;- t(x)<br>&gt; <br>&gt; heatmap(as.matrix(x_matrix,nrow(x_matrix),ncol(x_matrix)),Colv=NA)<br>&gt; <br>&gt; 1-How can I set colours based on LOD scores (-6 to -4 = green), (-4 to -2 blue), (-2 to 2 = white), (2 to 4 = yellow), (4 to 6 = red)?<br>&gt; 2- How to put a bar with colour scale?<br>&gt;  <br>&gt; Thanks in advance,<br>&gt;  <br>&gt; Mohamed<br>&gt;  <br>&gt; <br></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ],
